From 832e88b0c964a324bb09c7af02ed0650b73dfb9b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simon Ser <contact@emersion.fr>
Date: Sun, 21 Dec 2025 13:50:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] xdg_shell: skip configure in request_fullscreen handler if
 unmapped

wlr_xdg_surface_schedule_configure() requires the xdg_surface to
be initialized.

Closes: https://github.com/cage-kiosk/cage/issues/456

Upstream: https://github.com/cage-kiosk/cage/commit/832e88b0c964a324bb09c7af02ed0650b73dfb9b
[Backported to 0.2.1, where GStreamer's waylandsink sets this off: it
asks not to be fullscreen before its window's first commit.]
---
 xdg_shell.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/xdg_shell.c b/xdg_shell.c
--- a/xdg_shell.c
+++ b/xdg_shell.c
@@ -188,6 +188,10 @@
 {
 	struct cg_xdg_shell_view *xdg_shell_view = wl_container_of(listener, xdg_shell_view, request_fullscreen);
 
+	if (!xdg_shell_view->xdg_toplevel->base->surface->mapped) {
+		return;
+	}
+
 	/**
 	 * Certain clients do not like figuring out their own window geometry if they
 	 * display in fullscreen mode, so we set it here.
